step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a trimmed‑mean over the full pool to see if trimming improves over median and mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","models":["ARIMA","ETS","NaiveMovingAverage","FT_rf","DWT_catboost","FT_catboost","rf","catboost"],"trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a best_single strategy selecting ARIMA from the full pool to see if a single strong model outperforms the trimmed mean.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","pool":"pool_full","model":"ARIMA"}

Thought: Test a simple median over the high‑confidence pool1 to see if a robust statistic improves on the best single ARIMA.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the existing meta‑model weights (w1) but restrict it to the more stable pool2 to see if reduced variance improves performance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","models":["ARIMA","ETS","rf","FT_rf","DWT_catboost","FT_catboost"],"weights":"w1","rationale":"Use w1 on pool2"}

Thought: Test a DBA (distributional Bayesian averaging) on the small pool1 to see if a Bayesian ensemble improves over best ARIMA.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on pool2 using the w2 handle to see if a different weighting improves over the current leader.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","models":["ARIMA","ETS","rf","FT_rf","DWT_catboost","FT_catboost"],"weights":"w2"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using inverse_error weights on the strongest pool (pool5) to see if data‑driven weights beat the baseline w1/w2.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","models":["ARIMA","ETS","rf","FT_rf","DWT_catboost","FT_catboost"],"weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on pool2 using the inverse_error handle to see if focusing on the strongest models improves over the current best_single ARIMA.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a robust median over pool2 to see if a simpler pool improves over the weighted inverse-error baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool2"}

Thought: Test a plain mean over pool4 to see if a smaller pool improves over the current best single ARIMA.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","models":["ARIMA","ETS","rf","catboost","FT_rf","DWT_catboost"]}

Thought: Test a deterministic DBA ensemble on pool2 with 30 iterations to see if it improves over current best mean and weighted strategies.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool2","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a plain mean over pool4 to see if a slightly larger pool improves on the best single ARIMA.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool4"}

Thought: Test best_single ARIMA restricted to pool1 to see if a smaller pool improves performance over the full best_single strategy.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","pool":"pool1","model":"ARIMA"}

Thought: Test a best_single strategy using pool2 to see if a slightly larger pool improves on the current best single ARIMA.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","pool":"pool2","model":"ARIMA"}

Thought: Test a best_single ARIMA from pool3 to see if expanding the pool changes the best model choice.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","pool":"pool3","model":"ARIMA"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on pool3 to see if it beats the best single ARIMA.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"median","models":["ARIMA","ETS","rf","catboost","FT_rf","DWT_catboost"]}

